olatility":0.13519858555066616,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":75.7,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.034030310032493793,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":57.5,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.05729421318315886,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":62.9,"_gate_rev_durability":0.2017238818966598,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.022827366218794262,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":36.5,"_gate_share_shrink":0.096919933935246,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.008847599109486272,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":85.3,"_gate_insider_own":0.16845,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":1.0,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":100.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Mid Penn Bancorp, Inc. operates as the bank holding company for Mid Penn Bank that provides commercial banking services to individuals, institutional clients, partnerships, non-profit organizations, businesses, and corporations in Pennsylvania and New Jersey, the United States. The company offers various time and demand deposit products, including checking accounts, savings accounts, clubs, money market deposit accounts, certificates of deposit, and individual retirement accounts. It also provides a range of loan products comprising mortgage and home equity loans, secured and unsecured commercial and consumer loans, lines of credit, construction financing, farm loans, community development loans, loans to non-profit entities, and local government loans; and personal loans and lines of credit, home equity lines of credit, commercial lines of credit, commercial real estate financing, SBA loans, and agricultural loans. In addition, the company offers trust, retail investment, wealth management, and personal and business insurance services; private banking; insured cash sweep; debit, credit, and gift cards; online bill payment; and online and telephone banking, cash management, automated teller services, and safe deposit boxes. Mid Penn Bancorp, Inc. was founded in 1868 and is headquartered in Harrisburg, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Rory G. Ritrievi | President, CEO & Chairman | Age 61 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 721 people. Revenue per employee of $313K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 17%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $100K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Mid Penn Bancorp is a small-cap financial services business with a $894M market cap on $226M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years and +20% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $72M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 32 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.42\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.3% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 17% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 52% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","15 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Trading Systems Reacting to (MPB) Volatility","source":"news.sto